<node id="5G NAS security">
  <data key="entity_id">5G NAS security</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">5G NAS security refers to the security mechanisms applied in the 5G Non-Access Stratum layer to ensure confidentiality, integrity, and authentication during communication between the UE and the network. It includes the handling of 5G-EA0 for cryptographic operations.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-c3766b0bd2da84eace3065f40f55863c</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.2</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205635</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">5G NAS security</data>
</node>
<node id="KAMF derivation">
  <data key="entity_id">KAMF derivation</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">KAMF derivation is the process of generating a new KAMF, which triggers the resetting of downlink and uplink NAS COUNT to zero for non-3GPP access.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-7e397641e752f61c7495ea9622b8103c</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.2.3</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205745</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">KAMF derivation</data>
</node>
<node id="S1 mode to N1 mode NAS transparent container">
  <data key="entity_id">S1 mode to N1 mode NAS transparent container</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Technology</data>
  <data key="description">S1 mode to N1 mode NAS transparent container is a data container used in CONNECTED mode that carries NAS signaling information and is treated as an implicit SECURITY MODE COMMAND message for the UE and AMF.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-271beb7d1fe2c1b6d63a054506e7b878</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.3.1</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205776</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">S1 mode to N1 mode NAS transparent container</data>
</node>
<node id="SECURITY MODE COMMAND message">
  <data key="entity_id">SECURITY MODE COMMAND message</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">The SECURITY MODE COMMAND message is a signaling message sent by the AMF over one access to activate the same mapped 5G NAS security context on another access, used when the UE is in 5GMM-CONNECTED mode over non-3G&lt;SEP&gt;SECURITY MODE COMMAND message is a NAS message sent by the AMF to the UE to initiate or&lt;SEP&gt;SECURITY MODE COMMAND message is a control message used to initiate security mode procedures, and in CONNECTED mode, the S1 mode to N1 mode NAS transparent container is treated as an implicit instance of this message for both the UE and AMF.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-271beb7d1fe2c1b6d63a054506e7b878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdc80f9e0e79539377212798dce1ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3366856f62aa455b0deeeeb8040614</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.2.2&lt;SEP&gt;../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.2.6&lt;SEP&gt;../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.3.1</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205998</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">SECURITY MODE COMMAND message</data>
</node>
<node id="Replay protection">
  <data key="entity_id">Replay protection</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">Replay protection is a security feature that ensures a single NAS message is not accepted more than once by the receiver. It is required for received NAS messages in both the AMF and the UE. For a given 5G NAS security context, each NAS COUNT value must be accepted at most once and only if message integrity verification succeeds.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-1b7f566ef414e18b1d67b12d8cedbf12</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.3.2</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205804</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">Replay protection</data>
</node>
<node id="Integrity protection of NAS signall">
  <data key="entity_id">Integrity protection of NAS signall</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">Integrity protection of NAS signall is a security feature defined in section 4.4.4 that ensures the authenticity and integrity of Non-Access Stratum (NAS) signaling messages. It prevents unauthorized modification of NAS messages during transmission.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-87c075f0cf0189cf4a39f81e2c8777f4</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.4</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205916</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">Integrity protection of NAS signall</data>
</node>
<node id="NAS COUNT wrap around">
  <data key="entity_id">NAS COUNT wrap around</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">NAS COUNT wrap around is a condition detected by the AMF when either the downlink NAS COUNT or the uplink NAS COUNT is close to 224, triggering specific actions to maintain security and signaling integrity in the 5G network.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-7ddc7021e3bbd564e76be4d14fa69d8c</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.3.5</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205902</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">NAS COUNT wrap around</data>
</node>
<node id="CIoT small data container IE">
  <data key="entity_id">CIoT small data container IE</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Technology</data>
  <data key="description">CIoT small data container IE is an information element that contains a value part which shall be deciphered by the UE. The message handling follows the specification in subclause 5.6.1.4.2.&lt;SEP&gt;CIoT small data container IE is a specific information element used in CONTROL PLANE SERVICE REQUEST messages to carry non-cleartext data for CIoT (Cellular Internet of Things) services. It is ciphered only when it is the sole non-cleartext IE being sent.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-2cf58586d0687b7b5ca57670c605e12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e5e312e3142cb805667cbfa885449ce</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.6</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770205998</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">CIoT small data container IE</data>
</node>
<node id="initial NAS message">
  <data key="entity_id">initial NAS message</data>
  <data key="entity_type">Concept</data>
  <data key="description">The initial NAS message is the first NAS message&lt;SEP&gt;initial NAS message is a message sent by the UE that includes cleartext information elements only, transmitted via the access type associated with the&lt;SEP&gt;Initial NAS message is a signaling message sent by the NAS to initiate a procedure, such as a connection request, when needed after barring is alleviated.</data>
  <data key="source_id">chunk-2cf58586d0687b7b5ca57670c605e12e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b9ef174e9ae7d49b678ced2326c9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4810432d3228af17ae91a78cddb099e4</data>
  <data key="file_path">../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.2.5&lt;SEP&gt;../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.4.6&lt;SEP&gt;../3GPP-trunked/Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20.md4.5.4.1</data>
  <data key="created_at">1770206169</data>
  <data key="source_file">Rel-19/24_series/24501-j20/graph_chunk_entity_relation.graphml</data>
  <data key="release">Rel-19</data>
  <data key="raw_entity_id">initial NAS message</data>
</node>
